From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:28:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/38] Draw switches, sliders and progress views on Linux

Toggle and ProgressView crashed on Linux, where their styles ask UIKit for a
UISwitch or a UIProgressView, and Slider's system style drew nothing. They
are now drawn by SwiftUI with UIKit's sizes and colors: a 51 x 31 switch that
flips on a tap, a slider with a 28-point thumb that follows a drag and snaps
to its steps, a 4-point progress bar and a still activity indicator. Toggle
takes a title.
---
